WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.960
Going viral won't make you money, but

00:00:02.440 --> 00:00:05.960
this will. And I know that sounds

00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:08.880
backwards because everybody is chasing

00:00:05.960 --> 00:00:11.280
views, chasing followers, and obviously

00:00:08.880 --> 00:00:13.480
making money. But the truth that a lot

00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:15.240
of creators find out much further down

00:00:13.480 --> 00:00:17.840
the road is that you can get a million

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.680
views and make zero dollars. On the

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:22.200
other hand, a thousand views from the

00:00:19.680 --> 00:00:24.360
right viewers can completely change your

00:00:22.200 --> 00:00:25.800
business and your income. So, in today's

00:00:24.360 --> 00:00:28.000
video, I'm going to break down why you

00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:30.360
should not focus on going viral and what

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:32.439
exactly to do instead to create content

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:34.480
that actually converts to real money,

00:00:32.439 --> 00:00:36.880
whether you have 50 followers, 500

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:38.040
followers, or 50,000 followers. Most

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:40.640
creators are actually building their

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:41.880
content around the wrong metric. They're

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.800
often thinking, "How can I get more

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:45.120
views? How can I get more followers? How

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:47.400
do I go viral? How do I beat the

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:48.920
algorithm?" But very few creators are

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.760
actually asking the question that

00:00:48.920 --> 00:00:52.400
matters, which should be, "What do I

00:00:50.760 --> 00:00:54.040
want my audience to do after they're

00:00:52.400 --> 00:00:55.880
done watching?" And that question will

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:57.800
actually change everything. Because once

00:00:55.880 --> 00:00:59.320
you stop thinking like content creator

00:00:57.800 --> 00:01:01.120
and start thinking like a content

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.960
strategist, your content is actually

00:01:01.120 --> 00:01:04.680
going to become way more valuable, and

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:06.320
that is where you start making money.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:08.440
So, let's start with debunking the

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:10.360
biggest myth, which is that more views

00:01:08.440 --> 00:01:12.040
automatically means more money. But

00:01:10.360 --> 00:01:14.320
that's not always true. Of course, going

00:01:12.040 --> 00:01:17.120
viral can definitely help, but viral

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:19.200
attention is usually broad, random, and

00:01:17.120 --> 00:01:21.480
temporary. I can speak from experience

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:23.560
here because I actually had a video on

00:01:21.480 --> 00:01:25.440
this YouTube channel go viral several

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:27.600
years ago, actually a few months after I

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:30.040
initially started my channel. It did

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:33.160
make me money initially. I was making

00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:35.160
like 2,000 or so dollars per month when

00:01:33.160 --> 00:01:37.080
it initially was going viral, but the

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.680
reality is that it had this big bell

00:01:37.080 --> 00:01:40.520
curve and now I'm on the other end of

00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.320
that where I'm not actually making, you

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:44.480
know, $2,000 a month from my YouTube

00:01:42.320 --> 00:01:46.480
channel because that video is no longer

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:48.320
going viral. And the other downside to

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:50.160
this is that I started gaining followers

00:01:48.320 --> 00:01:51.720
that only cared about one specific

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:54.200
topic. They didn't actually care about

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:57.040
me as a content creator, and they didn't

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.320
necessarily trust everything that I said

00:01:57.040 --> 00:02:01.000
or what I had to offer. And that is the

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:03.200
key here. That is the difference between

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:05.080
attention versus conversion. Attention

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.440
means somebody looked at your content.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:08.119
However, conversion is what we really

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:09.720
want because conversion means that they

00:02:08.119 --> 00:02:11.640
took a look at your content and then

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:13.320
decided to do something about it. Maybe

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:14.920
they subscribed, they joined your email

00:02:13.320 --> 00:02:16.600
list, they booked a call, or more

00:02:14.920 --> 00:02:18.160
importantly, they bought your product.

00:02:16.600 --> 00:02:20.000
And this is where a lot of creators get

00:02:18.160 --> 00:02:21.760
stuck because they create a video and

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:23.640
then nothing happens afterwards. And

00:02:21.760 --> 00:02:25.400
that's because viral content is often

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:27.360
designed to get attention. But

00:02:25.400 --> 00:02:29.360
profitable content is designed to build

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:31.240
trust. So, here's the part that new

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.160
creators need to hear. You do not need a

00:02:31.240 --> 00:02:36.120
massive audience to make money. What you

00:02:33.160 --> 00:02:38.160
need is a specific audience. A small

00:02:36.120 --> 00:02:40.120
audience of the right people is way more

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:42.240
powerful than a large audience of people

00:02:40.120 --> 00:02:44.120
who just don't care. Think about it this

00:02:42.240 --> 00:02:46.160
way. Would you rather have 100,000

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:48.160
random people that watch your video or

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:49.680
1,000 people who are actively looking

00:02:48.160 --> 00:02:51.280
for a solution to the problem that

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:53.160
you're solving? If the people watching

00:02:51.280 --> 00:02:54.520
your video are way more targeted and

00:02:53.160 --> 00:02:56.240
you're actually solving a problem for

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:58.840
them, then they're way more likely to,

00:02:56.240 --> 00:03:00.880
again, convert and do something like

00:02:58.840 --> 00:03:02.360
subscribe to your email list, buy a

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:04.000
product that you're offering, sign up

00:03:02.360 --> 00:03:06.480
for a coaching call, or whatever the

00:03:04.000 --> 00:03:07.959
things that actually make you money. So,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:10.080
here's what you should do instead.

00:03:07.959 --> 00:03:12.160
Instead of asking, "How do I go viral?"

00:03:10.080 --> 00:03:13.959
start asking some of these questions.

00:03:12.160 --> 00:03:15.400
What problem does my audience have? What

00:03:13.959 --> 00:03:16.959
result are they trying to get? What do

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.920
they need to believe before they trust

00:03:16.959 --> 00:03:21.000
me? What action do I want them to take

00:03:18.920 --> 00:03:22.640
next? Answering those questions are how

00:03:21.000 --> 00:03:24.360
you're going to actually build content

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:26.760
that converts. Because the truth is that

00:03:24.360 --> 00:03:28.600
conversion does not actually happen by

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:30.920
accident. It happens when your content

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:32.680
creates a clear path. So, here is a

00:03:30.920 --> 00:03:34.280
simple framework that you can use. So,

00:03:32.680 --> 00:03:36.080
these are the four types of content that

00:03:34.280 --> 00:03:38.080
actually convert. The first one is

00:03:36.080 --> 00:03:39.280
problem-aware content. This is the type

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:41.560
of content that actually makes your

00:03:39.280 --> 00:03:42.959
audience feel super seen. It says, "I

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:44.040
understand what you're struggling with."

00:03:42.959 --> 00:03:46.160
For example, [clears throat] why your

00:03:44.040 --> 00:03:47.680
content gets views but no sales. This

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:49.239
type of content really works because

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:50.880
it's naming the pain. Somebody might be

00:03:49.239 --> 00:03:52.360
really frustrated that they are making

00:03:50.880 --> 00:03:54.240
awesome content but they're not actually

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:55.480
getting sales, right? A lot of creators

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.120
don't actually realize what the real

00:03:55.480 --> 00:03:59.280
problem is. They may be getting low

00:03:57.120 --> 00:04:01.440
views, when the real problem is unclear

00:03:59.280 --> 00:04:03.200
positioning, weak offers, or content

00:04:01.440 --> 00:04:05.000
that just doesn't lead anywhere. So,

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:07.040
problem-aware content gets people to

00:04:05.000 --> 00:04:08.920
stop and actually say, "Wait, that's me.

00:04:07.040 --> 00:04:10.320
You're targeting my problem and solving

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:11.600
a problem for me." And that's the

00:04:10.320 --> 00:04:13.560
beginning of how you actually build

00:04:11.600 --> 00:04:16.000
trust with your audience. Type two is

00:04:13.560 --> 00:04:17.560
educational content. This, obviously, is

00:04:16.000 --> 00:04:19.440
the type of content that teaches your

00:04:17.560 --> 00:04:21.359
audience something. For example, how to

00:04:19.440 --> 00:04:23.080
turn YouTube views into email

00:04:21.359 --> 00:04:24.160
subscribers. This is the type of content

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:26.000
where you can really show your

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:27.919
expertise. But, the key here is not to

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:30.120
just share random tips. You want to

00:04:27.919 --> 00:04:32.400
teach people in a way that moves people

00:04:30.120 --> 00:04:33.960
closer to their desired result. A lot of

00:04:32.400 --> 00:04:35.880
creators actually make the mistake of

00:04:33.960 --> 00:04:37.880
giving a lot of scattered advice. Maybe

00:04:35.880 --> 00:04:39.560
one day they share motivation. The next

00:04:37.880 --> 00:04:41.600
day they share productivity. Then a

00:04:39.560 --> 00:04:43.000
random trend. Then a personal story. I

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:44.560
actually did this a lot when I first

00:04:43.000 --> 00:04:46.160
created my YouTube channel. And,

00:04:44.560 --> 00:04:47.760
unfortunately, none of it connects. So,

00:04:46.160 --> 00:04:49.560
then when somebody does actually come to

00:04:47.760 --> 00:04:51.600
your YouTube channel or your TikTok page

00:04:49.560 --> 00:04:53.400
or whatever, none of it really is

00:04:51.600 --> 00:04:55.400
cohesive and it just doesn't make sense.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:57.120
But, educational content should build

00:04:55.400 --> 00:04:59.040
toward something and your audience

00:04:57.120 --> 00:05:00.840
should start to understand, "This person

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:02.720
really likes to help solve this problem

00:05:00.840 --> 00:05:04.640
for me." And that is when your content

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:06.720
really starts to become an asset. Type

00:05:04.640 --> 00:05:08.360
three is proof content. This is the type

00:05:06.720 --> 00:05:09.880
of content you all have probably seen

00:05:08.360 --> 00:05:12.360
here on YouTube where you actually share

00:05:09.880 --> 00:05:13.919
exactly how your strategy works. For

00:05:12.360 --> 00:05:15.680
example, you might have seen a YouTube

00:05:13.919 --> 00:05:17.760
video or something that claims something

00:05:15.680 --> 00:05:19.760
along the lines of, "How I make $10,000

00:05:17.760 --> 00:05:21.400
a month with digital products." I've

00:05:19.760 --> 00:05:23.160
made these types of videos on my channel

00:05:21.400 --> 00:05:26.000
as well, sharing things like, you know,

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:27.640
"How I gained my first 1,000 YouTube

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:29.000
subscribers." Now, of course, proof

00:05:27.640 --> 00:05:30.960
content does not mean you have to have

00:05:29.000 --> 00:05:32.600
some crazy huge success story. There's

00:05:30.960 --> 00:05:34.520
tons of different ways that you can show

00:05:32.600 --> 00:05:36.640
proof. It could be through things like a

00:05:34.520 --> 00:05:38.400
lesson learned, a mistake you fixed, a

00:05:36.640 --> 00:05:40.240
result you got, a comment from your

00:05:38.400 --> 00:05:41.560
audience, or a simple breakdown of

00:05:40.240 --> 00:05:42.960
something that happened. Proof,

00:05:41.560 --> 00:05:45.160
ultimately, builds credibility and

00:05:42.960 --> 00:05:46.760
credibility converts. The fourth type of

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:48.320
content that actually converts is called

00:05:46.760 --> 00:05:50.200
action content. This is the type of

00:05:48.320 --> 00:05:52.440
content where you tell people what to do

00:05:50.200 --> 00:05:54.480
next. For example, download this free

00:05:52.440 --> 00:05:56.040
content strategy checklist below. And

00:05:54.480 --> 00:05:58.040
this is actually how a lot of creators

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.320
lose money is they don't actually give

00:05:58.040 --> 00:06:02.520
people an actionable item to do, whether

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:04.240
it be a freebie or a paid item. They

00:06:02.520 --> 00:06:05.800
don't include a call to action, they

00:06:04.240 --> 00:06:07.400
don't mention their offer, and they

00:06:05.800 --> 00:06:09.280
don't connect their video to whatever

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:11.400
the next step might be. So, people may

00:06:09.280 --> 00:06:13.640
watch it, enjoy it, learn from it, and

00:06:11.400 --> 00:06:15.280
then leave. And unfortunately, that is

00:06:13.640 --> 00:06:16.440
just not how you're going to get paid.

00:06:15.280 --> 00:06:18.520
So, in order to do that, you need to

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:19.919
give your audience a clear next move.

00:06:18.520 --> 00:06:21.800
Now, that does not mean you have to be

00:06:19.919 --> 00:06:23.520
pushy, it just means you have to be

00:06:21.800 --> 00:06:25.120
intentional. A good call to action can

00:06:23.520 --> 00:06:26.760
be a few different things. For example,

00:06:25.120 --> 00:06:28.720
it could sound like subscribe for more

00:06:26.760 --> 00:06:30.440
videos like this. I usually say this at

00:06:28.720 --> 00:06:32.480
the end of all of my videos. Join my

00:06:30.440 --> 00:06:34.919
newsletter. Watch this next video if you

00:06:32.480 --> 00:06:36.400
want to learn more about X. Or, comment

00:06:34.919 --> 00:06:38.360
your biggest struggle. These are all

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:40.880
super easy actionable items that you're

00:06:38.360 --> 00:06:43.000
giving somebody a way to continue to

00:06:40.880 --> 00:06:45.240
stay engaged with your content and

00:06:43.000 --> 00:06:46.400
hopefully check out and buy something.

00:06:45.240 --> 00:06:48.280
All right, so let me give you an example

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:49.720
breakdown of how this all [music] kind

00:06:48.280 --> 00:06:51.520
of comes together. Let's say you're a

00:06:49.720 --> 00:06:52.880
creator and you make a video called

00:06:51.520 --> 00:06:54.800
"PLE, You're Trying to Start a

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:57.000
Business." It's funny, it's relatable,

00:06:54.800 --> 00:06:58.800
and it gets 500,000 views. There's no

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:00.520
clear offer, there's no next step,

00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:02.400
there's no deeper lesson. After the

00:07:00.520 --> 00:07:04.640
video, most people just laugh and

00:07:02.400 --> 00:07:06.720
scroll. Now, this other creator creates

00:07:04.640 --> 00:07:08.040
a video called "Three Mistakes Keeping

00:07:06.720 --> 00:07:10.480
Your Online Business From Making Its

00:07:08.040 --> 00:07:12.760
First $1,000." This video only gets

00:07:10.480 --> 00:07:14.440
8,000 views. Way fewer views, but on the

00:07:12.760 --> 00:07:16.600
plus side, the audience is way more

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:18.120
specific. The problem is clear and the

00:07:16.600 --> 00:07:20.080
creator is positioned as somebody who

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.720
actually knows and understands business

00:07:20.080 --> 00:07:23.160
growth. And at the end of the video,

00:07:21.720 --> 00:07:24.919
they say, "I put together a free

00:07:23.160 --> 00:07:27.520
checklist that shows you how to audit

00:07:24.919 --> 00:07:29.480
your offer, content, and sales page. You

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:31.480
can grab it below." Now, those 8,000

00:07:29.480 --> 00:07:33.560
views can turn into things like leads,

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:35.200
email subscribers, customers, or maybe

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:36.919
long-term followers. Because it was

00:07:35.200 --> 00:07:39.120
content that actually converts rather

00:07:36.919 --> 00:07:41.120
than focusing on going viral. So, let's

00:07:39.120 --> 00:07:43.440
focus on the real goal here. The real

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.600
goal is not to go viral. The real goal

00:07:43.440 --> 00:07:47.120
is to become valuable to a specific

00:07:45.600 --> 00:07:48.800
group of people. Because once your

00:07:47.120 --> 00:07:50.680
audience sees you as valuable,

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:52.080
everything changes. They start watching

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:53.880
more of your content, they start

00:07:52.080 --> 00:07:55.440
trusting your perspective, they start

00:07:53.880 --> 00:07:57.160
seeing you as the person who can help

00:07:55.440 --> 00:07:58.640
them. And when you eventually offer

00:07:57.160 --> 00:08:00.320
something, whether it be a product, a

00:07:58.640 --> 00:08:02.000
service, it will actually make sense to

00:08:00.320 --> 00:08:04.520
them, and more importantly, they'll be

00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:06.520
more likely to actually buy it. This is

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:08.800
why conversion-focused creators will

00:08:06.520 --> 00:08:10.160
always outperform viral creators

00:08:08.800 --> 00:08:11.760
financially. Because they're not

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:13.160
creating content built for attention,

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:15.560
they're creating content that's built to

00:08:13.160 --> 00:08:17.720
convert. So, here's the truth. A lot of

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:19.360
viral content is disposable. People

00:08:17.720 --> 00:08:21.440
watch it, react to it, and then,

00:08:19.360 --> 00:08:23.760
frankly, they forget it. But strategic

00:08:21.440 --> 00:08:25.840
content sticks. It solves a problem, it

00:08:23.760 --> 00:08:27.320
builds trust, it positions you clearly,

00:08:25.840 --> 00:08:29.600
and more importantly, it gives people a

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.960
reason to come back. So, stop measuring

00:08:29.600 --> 00:08:33.479
your success by only views, and start

00:08:31.960 --> 00:08:34.880
measuring it by better things. Are the

00:08:33.479 --> 00:08:36.800
right people finding you? Are they

00:08:34.880 --> 00:08:38.919
staying? Are they commenting with real

00:08:36.800 --> 00:08:40.400
questions? Are they joining your list?

00:08:38.919 --> 00:08:42.599
Are they curious about what you have to

00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:44.320
offer? That right there is real growth,

00:08:42.599 --> 00:08:46.240
not just viral growth. So, the next time

00:08:44.320 --> 00:08:47.720
you sit down to create content, don't

00:08:46.240 --> 00:08:49.640
ask yourself, "How can I make this go

00:08:47.720 --> 00:08:51.520
viral?" Instead, ask, "How can I make

00:08:49.640 --> 00:08:53.880
this valuable enough that the right

00:08:51.520 --> 00:08:55.160
person takes the next step?" Because

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:57.480
while going viral might get you

00:08:55.160 --> 00:08:58.880
attention, trust is what gets you paid.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:09:00.800
So, if this helped you rethink your

00:08:58.880 --> 00:09:03.160
content strategy, make sure you hit that

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:04.960
subscribe button for more videos on how

00:09:03.160 --> 00:09:06.400
to grow your audience, create content

00:09:04.960 --> 00:09:08.200
that converts, and building a creator

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.320
business that actually makes you money.

00:09:08.200 --> 00:09:11.000
All right, thank you guys so much for

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:12.826
watching this video, and I'll catch you

00:09:11.000 --> 00:09:14.846
in the next one.

00:09:12.826 --> 00:09:14.846
>> [music]

